    "content": "All 21 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core resume-building experience is solid: creating resumes, editing all content sections, template switching, section reordering/visibility/renaming, live preview, duplication with full data isolation, and title search with date sorting all work as specified.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-11** | **No persistence.** All work is lost on reload — created, edited, duplicated, renamed and deleted resumes revert to the 3 seeded demos. `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` are both empty; state is purely in-memory. |\n| **FT-19** | **Date filtering absent.** The dashboard has only a title search and a sort dropdown. No date inputs or range pickers exist anywhere, and date strings typed into search return \"No resumes found.\" |\n| **CS-21** | **Empty-title rename accepted.** The dashboard rename dialog saved a whitespace-only title, leaving a card with a blank heading and destroying the previous title. The editor rename path silently reverts with no feedback at all. |\n| **CS-9** | **No date-period validation.** An end date before the start date (`2020-03` → `2019-01`) and a future start date (`2030-05`) were both accepted with zero feedback, rendering \"May 2030 - Jan 2019\" in the preview. |\n| **CT-20** | **Minimal template drops the Summary heading.** The customized heading (\"About Me\") renders in Modern and Classic but is entirely omitted from the Minimal template's DOM, even though the summary content is visible. |\n\nTwo failures are notably high-impact: CS-11 makes the \"save multiple variations for different job applications\" goal unachievable beyond a single session, and CS-21 can silently destroy a resume's title with no way to recover it."
  }
